    "faq": {
      "description": "",
      "headline": "Frequently Asked Questions",
      "items": [{
  "description": "A site setting out survey translates the design drawings into physical points on the ground. It establishes the exact locations for buildings, roads, utilities, and other structures to ensure construction is accurate and complies with engineering plans.",
  "icon": "help-circle",
  "title": "What is a Site Setting Out Survey?"
}, {
  "description": "Without accurate setting out, structures can be misaligned or result in costly rework. SmartGrid Surveying ensures your project is built exactly as designed, maintaining legal and engineering compliance while saving time and resources.",
  "icon": "help-circle",
  "title": "Why do I need a Site Setting Out Survey?"
}, {
  "description": "The duration depends on the project size and complexity. SmartGrid Surveying provides a detailed timeline before starting, ensuring transparency. For example, a residential plot may take 1–2 days, while larger commercial or infrastructure sites may take several days.",
  "icon": "help-circle",
  "title": "How long does a Site Setting Out survey take?"
}, {
  "description": "Yes. SmartGrid Surveying places markers, pegs, or paint markings on the ground according to design coordinates, ensuring builders and contractors can accurately follow the plans.",
  "icon": "help-circle",
  "title": "Do you mark the site physically?"
}, {
  "description": "Absolutely. By aligning structures according to cadastral plans and approved drawings, SmartGrid Surveying ensures construction respects property boundaries, minimizing conflicts with neighbors or local authorities.",
  "icon": "help-circle",
  "title": "Can a Site Setting Out survey prevent boundary disputes?"
}, {
  "description": "After a site setting out survey, SmartGrid Surveying provides: \n\n\t 1. Survey drawings showing all marked points.\n 2. Coordinates of reference points.\n\t 3. Verification report confirming alignment with design.\n\t 4. Certificates for legal or regulatory purposes if needed.",
  "icon": "help-circle",
  "title": "What documentation do I get after the survey?"
}, {
  "description": "Initial marking is done before construction begins. SmartGrid Surveying recommends follow-up checks at key stages (foundation, floor slabs, road alignment) to maintain accuracy throughout the construction process.",
  "icon": "help-circle",
  "title": "How often should setting out checks be done?"
}, {
  "description": "Yes. SmartGrid Surveying operates under the Survey Act, Cap 299, and all work is performed by licensed surveyors. We also comply with county planning regulations and building codes.",
  "icon": "help-circle",
  "title": "Is this service compliant with Kenyan regulations?"
}, {
  "description": "You can contact SmartGrid Surveying via WhatsApp, email, or phone. We will schedule a site visit, provide a quotation, and outline the survey plan tailored to your project.",
  "icon": "help-circle",
  "title": "How can I request a Site Setting Out survey?"
}],
      "tag": "Common Questions",
      "type": "faq"
    },
