    "faq": {
      "description": "Straight answers from the field — the things clients ask us before commissioning their first survey.",
      "headline": "Frequently Asked Questions",
      "items": [{
  "answer": "Yes — and it's the cheapest insurance you'll ever buy. A topographical survey feeds your architectural designs, engineering plans, and county approvals, and it surfaces site realities (slopes, utilities, boundary positions) before they become costly change orders. Building on assumptions is the most expensive mistake in construction.",
  "question": "Do I need a survey before construction?"
}, {
  "answer": "Most projects take 1–3 days of fieldwork and 2–7 days of processing and drafting, depending on the size of the site, the terrain, and the deliverables you need. We confirm a clear timeline with your quotation — and flag any delays early, not at handover.",
  "question": "How long does a survey take?"
}, {
  "answer": "Yes. We use Ground Penetrating Radar (GPR) — including the LMX200 — alongside utility mapping techniques to locate buried water lines, power cables, and other infrastructure before you excavate. It protects your crew, your budget, and your programme.",
  "question": "Can you detect underground utilities?"
}, {
  "answer": "Boundary surveys start from KES 30,000+, topographical surveys from KES 50,000+, and drone mapping from KES 25,000+. Because every site is different, we price on size, terrain, and accessibility — request a custom quotation and we'll turn it around quickly.",
  "question": "How much will my survey cost?"
}, {
  "answer": "We're based in Nairobi (Ruiru) and work across Kiambu, Machakos, Kajiado, Mombasa, Kisumu, and Nakuru — with full crews regularly deploying to Uganda, Tanzania, Somalia, and the wider East Africa region.",
  "question": "Which areas do you cover?"
}, {
  "answer": "Professional, ready-to-use outputs: topographical maps and contours, boundary and cadastral plans, 3D point clouds, DEM/DSM models, CAD shapefiles, orthomosaics, volumetric reports, and signed survey reports — formatted for engineers, architects, and approval authorities.",
  "question": "What deliverables will I receive?"
}],
