    "faqs": {
      "cta": {
        "description": "Our team of experts is ready to assist you with your specific project requirements. Contact us today.",
        "headline": "Have more questions?",
        "href": "/contact",
        "label": "Contact Us"
      },
      "headline": "Frequently Asked Questions",
      "items": [{
  "answer": "A GPR (Ground Penetrating Radar) survey uses electromagnetic pulses fired into the ground to locate buried utilities, rebar, voids, and other subsurface features without excavation or drilling. The radar unit is pushed across the surface and the reflected signals are processed into a map showing the depth and position of detected features.",
  "question": "What is a GPR survey?"
}, {
  "answer": "Detection depth depends on soil type. In sandy or volcanic soils we typically achieve 3-8 meters of penetration, while wet clay heavily attenuates the signal and may limit depth to 1-2 meters. Where deeper targets are expected, we deploy lower-frequency antennas and combine GPR with electromagnetic locators.",
  "question": "How deep can GPR detect in Kenyan soil conditions?"
}, {
  "answer": "Yes. Concrete scanning is one of the most common GPR applications — we locate rebar, post-tension cables, conduits, and voids within slabs, walls, and beams quickly and without any damage to the structure.",
  "question": "Can GPR work through concrete?"
}, {
  "answer": "Preliminary findings and on-site markouts are provided immediately after scanning. Full interpreted reports and CAD drawings are delivered within the timeline agreed for your project — typically a few days depending on site size.",
  "question": "Do you provide same-day results?"
}, {
  "answer": "Completely safe. GPR emits low-power radio waves — there is no radiation risk to people, and the method is entirely non-destructive, making it ideal for occupied buildings, hospitals, and live industrial facilities.",
  "question": "Is GPR safe to use indoors?"
}, {
  "answer": "Our GPR teams are based in Nairobi and mobilize countrywide — Kiambu, Nakuru, Kisumu, Mombasa, and beyond — with most requests scheduled within 24 hours.",
  "question": "Do you offer ground penetrating radar surveys near me?"
}],
      "tag": "FAQs",
      "type": "faq"
    },
